A||||11||Ironhorse||Taillight of 85 Fiero GT||||6||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-11-2000||03:24 PM||||Hey ya'all.. I have a 85 Fiero GT and I'm wondering if there's anyway I can remove that black bars that goes up and down, and across the taillight. I don't like the way it looks and want to know if I can make it look clean without screwing it up... Is it plastic piece or is it a piece that is taped on there?  Thanks||||reg||6
Z||000001||Standard||04-11-2000||03:38 PM||||No way to remove it.  It's an integral part of the tail light.  I wanted to get rid of the on my 84 SC, but you basically have to break the tail light apart to get that grid out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-11-2000||04:02 PM||||Monkeyman knows the procedure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave85||04-11-2000||04:17 PM||||Basically it's black paint on the edges of the lens.  If you do the tail light sticker mod, you sand the black paint off the lens. That way you don't have lines going through what ever you have your stickers say.<P>I have Monkey's tail light mod, "Fiero GT" and it looks awesome!!!<BR>I can't show you a pic for 2 reasons,<BR>1, I don't have a digital camera and 2, my car is getting ready for paint and looks like guanno. As soon as it's done, I'll be posting pics.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ironhorse||04-11-2000||10:06 PM||||*lip synching to the tune of Shock the Monkey by Peter Gabriel*  oh hi Monkeyman heh heh the song isn't meant for you, REALLY HONEST!  Monkey, Dave85 and Fiero56 told me some really useful info about the taillight procedure. Could you please tell us hows it's done or your website if you have one.  I'll owe ya a banana  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Seriously Monkeyman, I would appreaciate it.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Ironhorse||04-11-2000||11:03 PM||||ok so I got the curiosity the best of me.. I went and took it apart and attempt to get the black grid off... I found that the fingernail  remover works... well works a little too well cuz it took off the grid and it made the surrounding plastic part looks terrible. Is there anything that will work but is a lot less harsher and kinder to plastic part of the taillight?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||04-12-2000||01:46 AM||||Oops, guess I was wrong... oh well, learn something new everyday..<P>Iron, if that stuff is harsh enough to take off fingernails no wonder it did a jobber on the plastic!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> &lt;grin&gt;||||reg||3
Z||000007||Monkeyman||04-12-2000||09:16 AM||||Technically I have a website on Darklords FIEROPROJECT page, but I haven't gotten around to sending him the info so he can start it for me.  As soon as I do, I'll post something about the black grid.||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||04-12-2000||06:24 PM||||I sanded the black paint off the innards of my taillights with a medium grade sandpaper, then progressively switched to finer grades until all the paint was gone and the plastic looked polished again. You have to be careful and take your time, but it does work.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||04-13-2000||01:24 AM||||Where I am inaccurate, I am at least <I>definitively</I> inaccurate.  In cases of major discrepancy it's always reality that's got it wrong.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000010||zeusrekning||04-13-2000||07:20 AM||||I sanded the grid off of mine with a block type finger nail file then painted the grid yellow with model car paint.||||reg||1
Z||000011||kong||04-14-2000||02:41 AM||||I left all the grids on mine when I put monkeys mods on my 87. But you have to remember that king kong was always caged after they took him from Skull island...hehe||||reg||1
